  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If an integer \\(n,\\) greater than \\(8,\\) is a solution of the equation \\(x^2-ax+b=0\\) and the representation of \\(a\\) in the base \\(n\\) numeration system is \\(18,\\) then the base \\(n\\) representation of \\(b\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(18\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(80\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(81\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(280\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "80"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1978-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "In ordinary notation, \\(a=(18)_n=n+8.\\) Since one root is \\(n,\\) the other root must be \\(8.\\) Their product is \\(b=8n,\\) whose base-\\(n\\) representation is \\(80.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Translate the base-\\(n\\) numeral \\(18\\) into \\(n+8\\)",
        "Use the sum and product of the two roots"
      ],
